  abstract = {A novel P2/tunnel/O3 ' composite Na0.7Bi0.01MnO2 cathode is developed via the Na+-site modification of Bi3+ in layer structure Na0.7MnO2 for the first time. Superior electrochemical performance with a high capacity retention of similar to 86.5\% after 300 cycles at 2C is obtained. Moreover, the tri-phase structure can also serve as a model material, which intuitively evidences the environmental structural stability order: tunnel {$>$} P2 {$>$} O3 '.},
